SPOILERS FOLLOW!























   Medusa's gaze attack is NOT linear. Without stealth, you would be turned to 
stone in each of the above.

>
>I assume you have to be blind to apply a mirror to Medusa - or is reflection
>enough?  If you're fast and stealthy, can you just sneak up on her and apply 
>the mirror with neither reflection nor blindness?  I'm not about to experiment
>on this one! ;^)

  A shield or amulet of reflection DOESN'T protect you from Medusa. If you're 
stealthy you can enter her room and destroy her with a mirror. 

  Simply advance to within exactly ONE SPACE of Medusa like this:


    #                          # |              |######### |   |   ##+    |
   -|---                       ##.              |          |<  |     |    |
   |@`.|                         -------------.--          -----     |    |
   |...############                    #     #              #        |    |
   |M``|                                                             ------
   -----

   Apply your mirror once. You get the message "Medusa is tired and doesn't 
look at your mirror". Medusa then advances toward you.


    #                          # |              |######### |   |   ##+    |
   -|---                       ##.              |          |<  |     |    |
   |@`.|                         -------------.--          -----     |    |
   |M..############                    #     #              #        |    |
   |>``|                                                             ------
   -----

   Apply the mirror again and she turns to stone.  If you try this you really
have to be careful because the mirror effect IS linear, but Medusa's attack
is NOT. If you wake her up and she is not in a direct line with you, you turn
to stone. I haven't found speed to be required for this to work but I would
recommend you have it anyway to be on the safe side. The danger is that there
seems to be a chance that Medusa may both advance and use her gaze attack in 
the same round. I've only found this to occur when I try this from more than 
one space away, though. Also watch out for squeeky board traps in the room.


